CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] .* move assignment: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] .* move construction: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] .* copy assignment: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] .* copy construction: SUCCESS$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
N5008 [class.copy.ctor]/15, [class.copy.assign]/13: an explicitly defaulted
copy or move constructor or assignment operator of a union copies the object
representation.  Their bodies stayed empty, so the assignment returned a
nondeterministic reference and nothing was copied (libstdc++ 16's
std::optional lost the value assigned).
